 The 5-year vision for VIREON is to transition from an open-source academic tool into the de facto standard for regulatory validation of neurotechnology.
 
 ## Phase 1: The Academic Standard
-Establish VIREON as the default benchmarking tool for BCI publications. Instead of publishing a static dataset, researchers will publish a `vireon-publications` Evidence Graph that can be instantly executed by peer reviewers to verify algorithmic claims.
+Establish VIREON as the default benchmarking tool for BCI publications. Instead of publishing a static dataset, researchers will publish a `vireon-publications (planned, not yet created)` Evidence Graph that can be instantly executed by peer reviewers to verify algorithmic claims.
 
 ## Phase 2: The Hardware Digital Twin Ecosystem
 Incentivize commercial amplifier and implant manufacturers to release "Black Box" `IPlugin` digital twins of their hardware. This allows developers to test against the specific noise profiles of devices (like the NeuroNexus or Blackrock arrays) without requiring the physical hardware on their desk.
@@ -12,4 +12,9 @@ Incentivize commercial amplifier and implant manufacturers to release "Black Box
 Achieve recognition by the FDA under the Medical Device Development Tools (MDDT) program. A company developing a new clinical decoder could run their algorithms through the VIREON adversarial validation suite, generate an immutable `IEvidence` bundle, and submit it directly to regulatory bodies as proof of safety and efficacy bounds.
 
